1.1.      “*Royalty*” means the monthly royalty payable in consideration of the licence of the SPAR Marks under clause 10.1 calculated as 2% (two per cent) of any revenues Aggregator collects and retains from Customer Orders (including, but not limited to, delivery fees and/or any service fees collected by Aggregator) plus taxes if applicable.

1.2.       The Aggregator must pay to SPAR (or SPAR’s designated Affiliate) the Royalty in a monthly payment transaction without any deduction or set-off other than as required by law within thirty (30) days of SPAR or its designated Affiliate’s invoice in Euros as of the last working day before the due date. In the event that there is a deficit after receipt of such payment, SPAR shall carry over said deficit due by Aggregator to reflect in the subsequent statement.

1.3.       If any such payments made by the Aggregator to SPAR (or SPAR’s designated Affiliate) under this Agreement constitute the whole or any part of the consideration for a taxable or deemed taxable supply by SPAR (or SPAR’s designated Affiliate), the Aggregator shall increase that payment by an amount equal to the VAT which is chargeable in respect of the taxable or deemed taxable supply in question, provided that SPAR (or SPAR’s designated Affiliate) shall have delivered a valid VAT invoice in respect of such VAT to Aggregator. If the Aggregator fails to comply with its obligations under this clause 11, it must pay on demand all interest and penalties which thereby arise to SPAR (or SPAR’s designated Affiliate). If any VAT invoice is delivered to the Aggregator after the relevant payment has been made, the Aggregator shall pay the VAT due within five (5) Business Days of SPAR delivering a valid VAT invoice.

 
{panel}

